from typing import ClassVar


class ContractNotes:
    USER_CREATE: ClassVar[str] = '**Phone inputs:** Optional nullable `phone` and `parent_phone` must match `^\\+[1-9][0-9]{1,14}$`: mandatory leading plus, nonzero first digit, 2–15 ASCII digits. Missing plus, whitespace, punctuation, empty strings and Unicode digits return 422; new inputs are not silently normalized. Students must supply at least one of `phone` or `parent_phone`; omitting both or setting both to null returns 422. Legacy response phone strings remain readable without rewriting stored values.'
    USER_SELF_UPDATE: ClassVar[str] = '**Phone input:** Nullable `phone` uses strict `^\\+[1-9][0-9]{1,14}$` validation (mandatory plus, 2–15 ASCII digits, nonzero first digit); noncanonical inputs return 422. Omitting `phone` preserves its stored value, including legacy representations; explicit null clears it only if a student retains another contact phone (otherwise 422). This self-update does not permit guardian destination fields.'
    USER_UPDATE: ClassVar[str] = '**Phone inputs:** Nullable `phone` and `parent_phone` use strict `^\\+[1-9][0-9]{1,14}$` validation; noncanonical inputs return 422. Omitted fields retain stored values; explicit null clears them only if a student retains at least one contact phone (otherwise 422). Replacing an otherwise-valid historical optional-plus parent number with the same canonical number preserves the linked Telegram guardian. Real parent-number changes or clearing revoke the prior binding unless an authorized explicit guardian destination is supplied. Historical comparison accepts only 2–15 ASCII digits with optional plus; malformed stored numbers are not normalized or equated with null. Output phone strings remain permissive for legacy reads.'
    JOURNAL_HISTORY_PAGE: ClassVar[str] = '**History bounds:** `page_size` defaults to 20 and must be between 1 and 100. `course_id`, when provided, must name a nondeleted enrollment belonging to the authenticated student; otherwise the response is 403. Unknown query fields and malformed, modified, cross-student or cross-filter cursors return 422.\n`next_cursor` is `string | null`; null means the bounded traversal has no remaining page. Cursors bind the student, course filter, started-only setting and date cutoff. Pages sort by `period_start DESC, journal_id DESC`. `started_only=true` freezes the school-date cutoff across pages. `has_upcoming_periods` reports whether an eligible period starts after the current school date, without returning future history; ownership and the course filter apply to this flag.\nThe legacy `/students/me/journals` array preserves complete responses for at most 100 periods and returns 409 on overflow; it never silently truncates. Clients must migrate navigation and chart windows before releasing histories exceeding that limit. Course-wide totals come from existing profile aggregates, not a partial history page.'
    JOURNAL_AUTOSAVE: ClassVar[str] = '**Autosave bounds:** The request remains a top-level JSON array with 0–250 entries. Empty arrays are accepted as no-ops.\nEvery normalized `(student_id, lesson_date)` pair must be unique; identical and conflicting duplicate keys both return 422 before service work.\nEach optional nullable comment is limited to 1000 Unicode code points; longer comments return 422 without truncation.\nActual HTTP request bodies exceeding 4,194,304 bytes return 413 before JSON decoding, including chunked requests or misleading Content-Length headers.\nOnly this PUT route is capped; document and image upload limits are unchanged.\nAccepted batches retain existing partial-conflict, optimistic-version and idempotent retry behavior.'
    ORG_SETTINGS_UPDATE: ClassVar[str] = '**Input keys:** Only `org_name`, `notify_payments` and `notify_debts` are accepted (`additionalProperties: false`). Any unknown key returns 422 for the whole request without applying its other fields.'
    MENTOR_PROFILE: ClassVar[str] = 'Students receive only public mentor identity and course identity for their nondeleted enrollments on nondeleted courses belonging to this nondeleted mentor. Historical enrollment statuses remain eligible. The `active_courses` name is retained for caller compatibility; it does not impose an active enrollment or course status filter. No contact, DOB, parent, account metadata, full course details or mentor-wide statistics are returned. The response union is `MentorProfileResponse | StudentMentorCardResponse`; the staff response above is unchanged. Students without an eligible relationship, unrelated mentors and accountants receive 403.'
